  "data": {
    "body": "The Alternating Series Test shows that \n$\\sum_{k=1}^\\infty (-1)^k \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5k}}$\nconverges to a value S.\nSet\n$S_N = \\sum_{k=1}^N (-1)^k \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5k}} $\nFind the smallest N, using The Estimation Theorem for Alternating Series, such that we can conclude\n$|S-S_N| < \\frac{1}{10^2}$",
    "solution": [
      2
    ],
